---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/support-pages.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Commercial Refrigeration Training for HVAC Technicians | HVAC Training Solutions" description="Explore Ron Walker's existing commercial refrigeration course for working HVAC technicians. Ask about current availability and enrollment.">
  <div class="support-page">
    <section class="support-hero"><div class="support-shell">
      <p class="support-eyebrow">For experienced HVAC technicians</p>
      <h1>Move into commercial refrigeration.</h1>
      <p class="support-lead">This existing course was created for residential HVAC technicians who want to understand commercial refrigeration systems.</p>
    </div></section>
    <section class="support-section"><div class="support-shell support-split">
      <div class="support-heading"><p class="support-eyebrow">Course overview</p><h2>Build on what you already know.</h2><p>The original course compares residential HVAC with commercial refrigeration. Its described topics include the refrigeration cycle, metering devices, walk-in and reach-in equipment, defrost methods, and troubleshooting.</p></div>
      <div class="resource-list">
        <article><span>01</span><div><h3>Video-based lessons</h3><p>The course page describes videos alongside textbook study.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>02</span><div><h3>Refrigeration equipment</h3><p>Connect system principles to coolers, freezers, controls, and field problems.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>03</span><div><h3>Confirm current details</h3><p>Ask about course availability, required textbook, current support, price, and enrollment before purchase.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="support-section support-section-soft"><div class="support-shell support-next-step"><div><p class="support-eyebrow">Interested in refrigeration training?</p><h2>Talk with Ron about the course.</h2><p>This original page address is preserved. We are reviewing the current scope and enrollment details during the site rebuild.</p></div><a class="button button-primary" href="/contact/">Ask about the course</a></div></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
